{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p4-99ff645c","text":"So the About hero uses PageHeader with `background={stageGroup}` (faint background photo behind the navy) and an `aside` with a photo card (chapterAudience). The user wants: remove the pictures, leave the background in the About page hero — i.e., keep the navy background but remove the images (both the background photo behind the hero and the aside photo card?). "remove the pictures there and leave the background" — I read it as: remove the pictures [the photo card on the right], and leave the background [the navy gradient]. Actually attached screenshot shows the hero with the right-side photo. They said "in the about page the image attached remove the pictures there and leave the background". Ambiguous but reasonable: remove images so just the navy background remains with the heading. I'll remove both the aside photo card and the background image (stageGroup) so the hero is pure navy/wash. Hmm—"leave the background" could mean keep the faint background image. The screenshot shows a dark navy hero with a faint background photo of people and a bright photo card on right. "remove the pictures there and leave the background" most plausibly: delete the images; keep the (navy) background. I'll remove both `background` and `aside`, letting the title use the full width. Let me check PageHeader to see behavior without background/aside.

Third request: "wait is that all the design you can do on the website i am talking about hover reveal effects and blah blah blah" — they want richer hover/reveal effects. So add tasteful hover/motion polish across the site.

Fourth: "have you test all the login users and all the functionality???" — they want verification that logins work. There's seed data with admin@glance.org.ng / agent ChangeMe!2026 etc. Testing logins requires the DB running and dev server. That's a big task. In this turn I should: (1) remove theglanceproject.org link from about page, (2) remove images from about hero, (3) add hover reveal effects polish, (4) test logins.

The login testing is substantial — requires DB. Historical context: there's a local DB start script (scripts/start-local-db.ps1) and .tmp reset-demo-data.mjs. It's big; but user demands it. I should focus this turn mainly on the removals + effect polish, and actually attempt login testing via HTTP on the dev server (curl the login POST server action? Server actions are hard to curl). Alternative: use the browser preview tools to actually log in with seeded users and screenshot. That's feasible: preview_open localhost, use login page, type credentials, submit.

Given size, plan with todos. Let me set up todos and proceed.

