All done — here's everything, one by one.

## 1. The readability bug — fixed at the root

The mobile menu wasn't just "lightly styled": it had a real bug. The drawer gets its dark-look colors via a CSS remap that only targeted *elements inside* the drawer — the drawer's own white background was never remapped. So every label was remapped to near-white **on a white background** — literally invisible. One-line fix in [globals.css](src/app/globals.css) (`drawer-dark.bg-white`): the drawer now renders as a navy surface with bold white headings, and in the live preview I opened this menu and every item is crisp. That same root cause was why it looked "impossible to read" every time, not just faint.

## 2. Bug/lag sweep across the site & login

- **Mobile menu drawer** — fixed (above).
- **Login flow, end to end** — verified live in the browser, not just read: officer sign-in → portal → **"Welcome back"**; chapter-admin sign-in → lands straight in its own chapter portal with zero profile-gate; sign-out works. Failed sign-ins are logged and rate-limiting is server-side.
- **Seed accounts** — the chapter-admin and comms-manager accounts existed but had stale password hashes from an earlier run, so logins would have failed silently. The new seed ([scripts/seed.ts](scripts/seed.ts)) now owns these three passwords idempotently, sets them to ACTIVE/verified, and marks them profile-complete so they're never blocked at sign-in.
- **Film/reel embeds** — already click-to-load from the previous fix; re-confirmed 0 iframes at rest, exactly 1 when playing.
- **Database connection** — the live Supabase pooler dropped connections mid-session twice today (transient network flaps); the app already retries transient failures in [db.ts](src/server/db.ts). This is a *watch item* for production, not a code bug — a pooled connection with `connection_limit` is already in place.

## 3. Login details (ready now, verified working)

| Account | Portal name | Email | Password |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **GLANCE Network Officer** | GLANCE Network Officer | `officer@glance.org.ng` | `Glance!Officer2026` |
| **Communications Manager** | Communications | `comms@glance.org.ng` | `Glance!Comms2026` |
| **Chapter Admin** (demo) | Chapter coordinator | `chapteradmin@demo.glance.org.ng` | `Glance!ChapterAdmin2026` |

All at `/portal/login`. Chapter admin (demo) belongs to "GLANCE Club, Demo University (GLNDEMO1)" — a demo chapter. On production, chapter admins for real chapters aren't a fixed login — they're created by the officer (next point).

## 4. Network officer → creates Chapter Admins (as you wanted)

Yes, that's the designed flow, verified in the code and settings:

1. Cluster sends in a chapter application form (or the officer creates the chapter directly).
2. The officer approves it on the Applications page — the system **automatically creates the chapter and sends a CHAPTER_ADMIN invitation** to the contact email (or the officer can invite manually on the Invitations page, role “Chapter coordinator,” for any existing chapter).
3. That person opens the invitation email, sets a password at `/portal/activate`, and is a chapter admin on first sign-in — with their access scoped to *only their* chapter enforced server-side on every action.

## 5. Deploying to Vercel — step by step

I wrote the full runbook in [DEPLOY-VERCEL.md](DEPLOY-VERCEL.md). The short version:

1. Push the code to GitHub.
2. In Vercel, **Add New → Project → select the repo** (it auto-detects Next.js).
3. Before deploying, set env vars in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables — at minimum: `DATABASE_URL` (pooled Postgres connection, e.g. your Supabase pooler URL with `?sslmode=require&connection_limit=5`), `DIRECT_URL` (non-pooled direct URL — needed only for migrations), `SESSION_SECRET` (a fresh long random string), `APP_ORIGIN` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN` (`https://<your-domain>`), `BREVO_API_KEY`/`BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL`/`INVITE_EMAIL_NAME`, `CLOUDINARY_*`, and optionally the `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_*` pair. Set them for **Production, Preview and Development** scopes.
4. Deploy. Run `npx prisma migrate deploy` against the prod database once (from your machine), then `npx tsx scripts/seed.ts` with `SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL`/`SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD` set — **do not** set `GLANCE_SEED_DEMO=true` on prod, that creates the Demo University chapter and demo accounts.
5. Point the domain: Vercel → Domains → `A @ 76.76.21.21` + `CNAME www → cname.vercel-dns.com`, then bump `APP_ORIGIN` to the final HTTPS domain.
6. Post-deploy checks: `/` renders; `/portal` redirects to `/portal/login`; log in as the officer; submit a join application; publish a media item; confirm an invitation email arrives. Every git push re-deploys automatically.

## 6. architecture.md — brought up to date and expanded

[architecture.md](architecture.md) now includes: a corrected stack entry (Postgres via Prisma on Supabase — Aiven also fine), the exact seed-account table with the default passwords and how to override them, DEPLOY-VERCEL.md as the cross-referenced runbook, documented the click-to-load media player (explaining why the reel poster is a branded card, not a scraped thumbnail), and the session-store design (DB-backed session check on every request). The roles matrix and security model sections were verified against the actual code.

## 7. What still needs doing/fianlizing before deployment

- **Demo accounts on prod** — don't seed them; create the officer/comms passwords you want, then officer creates the real chapter-admin accounts via invitations.
- **Brevo setup end-to-end** — confirm the sender domain is fully verified and set `BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL`. Test one invitation email from the portal during deployment.
- **Cloudinary** — passwords are strong but nothing rotates them automatically; suggest enabling 2FA in the Cloudinary dashboard and Brevo, and rotating `SESSION_SECRET` at the same time as the first prod deploy.
- **PostHog** — project token/host pair is needed if you want analytics live; otherwise leave the env pair blank and the client simply never loads.
- **Footer/contact details** — `info@glance.org.ng` shown in the footer and in a few text blobs should be confirmed as a real inbox before shipping.
- **News/articles** currently render head tags only from post titles; if you want OG images, adding `openGraph` metadata per post would be nice-to-have.

