{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p11-64fe9457","text":"Committed (no attribution trailer, per user preference). Done. Final answer: explain cause, fix, verification results, the preview-tool caveat, and note they need to push to see it on GitHub (one commit ahead now — they can push). Also note test it: open site in own browser → banner; dismiss; click Home/reload → no banner; new tab → banner again.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
Fixed — the welcome banner now shows exactly **once per browser session**, not every time you come back to Home.

**What was happening:** the banner's "already shown" marker was stored in page memory only. That memory dies on every full page load — every refresh, every time you open `localhost:3001` again, every dev-server restart. So the banner greeted you again as if it was your first visit, and clicking Home after one of those reloads replayed it. The "don't replay during browsing" part worked (I verified with a canary token that Home clicks were client-side, no reload), but the moment anything did a full load, the marker was gone.

**The fix** (committed in `adc5222`):
- [cinematic-intro.tsx](src/components/site/cinematic-intro.tsx) now writes the "welcomed" marker to `sessionStorage` when you press Enter. That marker lives as long as the tab is open — through reloads, navbar clicks back to Home, and full page loads — and clears itself when the tab closes, so the next time you open the site it welcomes you again. That's exactly the "show once when you load the website" behavior you asked for.
- [layout.tsx](src/app/layout.tsx) — the pre-paint gate (the script that hides the homepage behind the banner before first paint) now reads the same marker, so it doesn't hide a page for a banner that isn't playing. I also added a defensive release in the intro component so the homepage stage can never get stuck hidden.

**Verified in the running browser:** a fresh session shows the banner; after dismissing it, clicking out to News and back Home via the navbar shows no banner; reloading home with the marker set keeps the page fully visible (no blank stage); typecheck passes and the console is clean. One tooling note: the built-in preview browser I test with has a quirk where it resets site storage on its own reload button — in your normal browser (Chrome/Edge/Firefox), `sessionStorage` persists across reloads within a tab, which is what makes this fix work. If you want the banner to never come back even in a brand-new tab (truly once ever), that's a one-line change to `localStorage` instead.

Your machine's tab will still show the banner one more time when you reopen the site — that's the first fresh session after the fix. After that you're set.

The commit is local (one commit ahead of origin) — `git push --force origin master`... actually plain `git push origin master` is enough now, since the rewritten history is already on GitHub.
