2. The scroll-close listener: on mobile the page scroll happens on document/window — scrolling closes the menu, so the user barely sees it.

3. Most critically in screenshot: the menu items are clipped horizontally *off the left edge*. When the ⋯ button is near the left edge of a card and `right-0` would place the menu's right edge at the button's right — hmm, actually `right-0` aligns menu's right edge with wrapper's right edge, so the menu extends leftward from the button. If the button is at x=100 and the menu is 190px wide, the menu starts at x=-90 → off-screen left. That's exactly the "cut off, half hidden" issue in the screenshot ("ending" clipped words at the left screen edge).

Also possible vertical clipping: rows have `overflow-hidden`? The applications page cards might have `overflow-hidden` on the card container, clipping the dropdown. In screenshot 1 the ⋯ button is at the bottom-left of the card and the menu doesn't appear at all (maybe overflow-hidden clipping or scroll-close closed it instantly). "most of the 3 dots menu are buried down and can't be seen at all on mobile" — could be the menu opens below the fold AND the scroll-close… or `overflow-hidden` clipping.

The robust fix: position the menu with `fixed` coordinates computed from the trigger's bounding rect, clamped to the viewport (typical "click outside viewport clamp" pattern). Also don't close on scroll (or only close when scrolled far), and give rows no overflow-hidden clipping… simpler: render menu via portal? Keep it simple: compute fixed position on open:

- rect = trigger.getBoundingClientRect()
- menuWidth = 200; estimate height = items*42 + 12 (cap ~260)
- left = clamp: prefer align right edge with rect.right if fits; else left edge; clamp within 8px margins
- top = rect.bottom + 6; if overflows bottom, open upward (rect.top - height - 6), clamp min 8.

Use fixed positioning with a small state for coordinates, set after open via rAF. Also listen to resize/close on scroll beyond some threshold... scroll-close was deliberate. On mobile, scrolling the page scrolls the fixed menu with content? No — fixed stays. If we no longer close on scroll, the menu would stay anchored to viewport while the row scrolls away — still visible and actions still targetable. Better: keep close-on-scroll only when scrollY delta > 80px? On mobile a single touch scroll usually exceeds that immediately, so keep closing. Actually the "buried down" complaint: the ⋯ at the bottom row opens a menu that extends below viewport bottom — invisible. With upward flip fix, solved. And left-edge clipping solved by clamping.

