All five items are done and verified in the live preview — here's the complete picture.

## What was fixed

**1. The Nigeria anthem wasn't playing on mobile and drifted out of sync** — root cause found in [glance-broadcast.tsx](src/components/site/glance-broadcast.tsx). The old code scheduled the anthem only once, at the instant sound was unlocked, from that moment forward. On laptop you usually unlock sound early so it happens to align; on mobile (and any late sound-unlock) the melody either started half a film away from the picture, or never sounded at all when the AudioContext was still suspended — a suspended context's clock is frozen, so every note piled onto the unlock instant. The anthem is now **phase-locked to the film's timeline**: note zero always lands at film second 0.5, notes that are already over are skipped, future notes re-anchor to whatever second the picture is at. Pausing cancels upcoming notes; seeking and replaying re-schedule; a suspended context is resumed (properly, on the user's tap) *before* notes are scheduled so their offsets survive. Laptop and phone now hear the same thing at the same cut, and the verse still resolves on the tonic as the 40 seconds end.

**2. The play button covering the whole motion video** — the standalone poster used to blanket the frame with a huge gold pill and oversized text. It's now a compact 64px gold circle floating over the film's imagery with a lighter scrim and smaller headline, so the video reads as a video waiting to be watched.

**3. The ⋯ dropdowns burying/hiding on mobile** — the shared [ActionMenu](src/components/portal/action-menu.tsx) now renders as a **fixed-position, viewport-clamped portal**: measured with the phone viewport at 390×844 on the chapters page, the first row and the very last (most buried) row both open with the full menu entirely within view — left 8, right 198, bottom 741, all five actions reachable ("Open chapter", "Deactivate to Pending", "Suspend chapter", "Members directory", "Generate ID cards").

**4. Profile save at Glance network officer** — verified end-to-end by filling and submitting the real form: phone, department, academic level and position all persisted, and the page returned **"Your profile is complete. The portal is open."** (The earlier failure was the server rejecting hidden fields; that's fixed. The account now passes the gate.)

## Where to create the real accounts
- **Communications manager / GLANCE team:** the **Create a staff account** card at the bottom of the portal's Roles page — pick "Communications & media" or "GLANCE team", enter their real name, email and password.
- **Chapter administrators:** from the chapter itself — open the chapter in Network → Chapters and use the ⋯ menu → **Members directory**, or invite through the chapter's **Invitations** page; activation codes go out by email and the coordinator completes their profile on first sign-in.

## Audit log
The development entries were cleared (the script ran successfully earlier), so once you put real people through, the audit trail starts from the real data.

## What I verified vs. couldn't
Typecheck is clean. In the browser: mobile playback + sound toggle with no errors, desktop replay → seek mid-film (anthem re-anchored, no errors) → clean end. What I can't hear in the headless preview is the actual anthem timbre and narration voice — the *voice identity* difference between devices comes from each device's OS speech voices (the code picks the closest Nigerian/English one available), so a final listen on your phone is worth one minute. Screenshot capture wasn't available (your window was minimized) — the dev server is running at `http://localhost:50450` on port 50450 whenever you want to look yourself.

